        <label>Queue Found and Is Owner?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Queue Not Found Or Not Owner</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Queue_Found</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>rec_Queue</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.OwnerId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <elementReference>rec_Queue.Id</elementReference>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Queue_Members</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Queue Found</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Are_Members_Found</name>
        <label>Any Queue Members?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Members</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Members_Found</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>col_Members</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Loop_Group_Members</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Members Found</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Is_Group_Member_A_User</name>
        <label>Is Group Member a User?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Loop_Group_Members</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Not a User</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Is_User</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Loop_Group_Members.UserOrGroupId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>StartsWith</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>005</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Add_User_Id</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Is User</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Are_Active_Users_Found</name>
        <label>Any Active Users?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Active Users</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Active_Users_Found</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>col_Users</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Email_Template</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Active Users Found</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Is_Template_Found</name>
        <label>Template Found?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Template Not Found</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Template_Found</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>rec_Template</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Loop_Users</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Template Found</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>After-save flow (Create only) that notifies every active member of the Investor Onboarding Queue by email when a new Investor Onboarding Lead lands in that queue. Pairs with IR_Lead_Assignment_Flow, which reassigns OwnerId to the queue in a BEFORE-save flow on the same Create -- because that assignment commits before this after-save flow&apos;s entry criteria evaluates, $Record.OwnerId already reflects the queue owner here. Scoped to Create only so a queue member taking ownership of the Lead later (an Update) does not re-trigger a notification. ENTRY CRITERIA: the ideal single-formula check {!$Record.Owner:Group.DeveloperName} = &apos;Investor_Onboarding_Queue&apos; was attempted first and rejected at deploy time (&quot;Group is an invalid object type for the Owner field&quot;) -- Lead.Owner does not support the polymorphic safe-navigation cast in a Flow start filterFormula in this org/API version. The entry criteria is therefore deliberately COARSE -- AND(RecordType.DeveloperName = &apos;Investor_Onboarding&apos;, LEFT(CASESAFEID(OwnerId), 3) = &apos;00G&apos;), i.e. record type plus &quot;owned by some queue&quot; -- and the precise check (owned by THIS queue) is done inside the flow by Is_Queue_Found, whose rule requires BOTH rec_Queue to be non-null AND $Record.OwnerId to equal rec_Queue.Id. This is why the queue is still looked up here even though IR_Lead_Assignment_Flow already resolved it moments earlier in a separate flow interview -- entry-criteria formulas cannot pass values into a flow&apos;s own elements, and this flow needs the queue&apos;s Id anyway for the GroupMember query. Resolves the queue by Group.DeveloperName (&apos;Investor_Onboarding_Queue&apos;) AND Group.Type (&apos;Queue&apos;) and the template by EmailTemplate.DeveloperName (&apos;IR_Lead_Notification_Email&apos;) -- never a hardcoded Id. Sends one email per active queue-member User rather than one email to the group, because the &quot;Send Email&quot; core action&apos;s recipientId only accepts a single Lead/Contact/User/person-account Id, not a Group Id. Fails closed at every stage: if the queue (or ownership match), its members, an active user among them, or the template cannot be resolved, the flow simply ends without sending. DELIBERATE: the email template carries no Lead merge fields -- see IR_Lead_Notification_Email&apos;s body for the full measured reason (an emailSimple send to a User recipientId cannot also carry a Lead relatedRecordId in this org, confirmed HTTP 400).</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>IR Lead Notification Flow {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>IR Lead Notification Flow</label>
    <loops>
        <name>Loop_Group_Members</name>
        <label>Loop Group Members</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <collectionReference>col_Members</collectionReference>
        <iterationOrder>Asc</iterationOrder>
        <nextValueConnector>
            <targetReference>Is_Group_Member_A_User</targetReference>
        </nextValueConnector>
        <noMoreValuesConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Active_Users</targetReference>
        </noMoreValuesConnector>
    </loops>
    <loops>
        <name>Loop_Users</name>
        <label>Loop Users</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <collectionReference>col_Users</collectionReference>
        <iterationOrder>Asc</iterationOrder>
        <nextValueConnector>
            <targetReference>Send_Notification_Email</targetReference>
        </nextValueConnector>
    </loops>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Investor_Onboarding_Queue</name>
        <label>Get Investor Onboarding Queue</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Is_Queue_Found</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>DeveloperName</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Investor_Onboarding_Queue</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Type</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Queue</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>Group</object>
        <outputReference>rec_Queue</outputReference>
        <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Queue_Members</name>
        <label>Get Queue Members</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Are_Members_Found</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>GroupId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>rec_Queue.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>false</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>GroupMember</object>
        <outputReference>col_Members</outputReference>
        <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
        <queriedFields>UserOrGroupId</queriedFields>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Active_Users</name>
        <label>Get Active Users</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Are_Active_Users_Found</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>In</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>col_UserIds</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>IsActive</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>false</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>User</object>
        <outputReference>col_Users</outputReference>
        <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Email_Template</name>
        <label>Get Email Template</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Is_Template_Found</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>DeveloperName</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>IR_Lead_Notification_Email</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>EmailTemplate</object>
        <outputReference>rec_Template</outputReference>
        <queriedFields>Id</queriedFields>
    </recordLookups>
    <start>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Get_Investor_Onboarding_Queue</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterFormula>AND({!$Record.RecordType.DeveloperName} = &apos;Investor_Onboarding&apos;, LEFT(CASESAFEID({!$Record.OwnerId}), 3) = &apos;00G&apos;)</filterFormula>
        <object>Lead</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Create</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
